  "configuration_id": "config_013",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only multiprofile with scvi_n200 is the clear winner (acc 0.653), and we've mapped the RNA encoder ranking (scvi > pca > scgpt) and confirmed aggregation barely matters. However, the image modality is essentially unexplored—config_010 (resnet50, singleprofile) scored only 0.208, near chance. The critical uncertainty is whether a stronger image encoder (ViT-L) can extract any useful signal from the images, or whether the image modality is simply uninformative for this task. Question: config_013 (image_only, singleprofile, imagenet_vit_l) is a clean single-variable comparison to config_010 (only the image encoder changes from resnet50 to ViT-L), isolating the effect of representation quality on image signal. Why this is the best next experiment: Before investing limited budget in multimodal fusion experiments (configs 016-051), we need to know whether image carries any discriminative information at all. If ViT-L image remains near chance, we can rule out the image modality entirely and focus remaining budget on RNA refinements. If it shows meaningful signal, multimodal fusion becomes a high-value direction. This experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the most consequential design decision (include image or not) with a minimal, interpretable comparison."
}

